id: k8s.endpoints
kind: kubernetes
title: Endpoints and EndpointSlice
aliases: endpoints, endpointslice
tags: networking, diagnostics
questions:
  - a service returns connection refused, where do you look first?
invariant: The endpoint list is the actual set of Pod IPs traffic is sent to, derived from the selector plus readiness.
answer_30s: Endpoints (now EndpointSlices) are the Pod IPs behind a Service; an empty list means no ready Pod matches the selector.
answer_2m: |
  This object is the fastest way to separate network problems from workload
  problems: if endpoints are present, the Service and selector are correct and
  the fault is in the Pod or the data path; if endpoints are empty, the fault
  is a label mismatch, a failing readiness probe, or Pods that are not running.
  EndpointSlice is the scalability replacement (bounded object size) and is
  what modern clusters and meshes actually read.
when_to_use:
  - first diagnostic step for any "service not reachable" report
commands:
  - kubectl get endpoints api => is traffic going anywhere at all
  - kubectl get endpointslice -l kubernetes.io/service-name=api => the modern equivalent, with ready conditions
  - kubectl describe endpoints api => which addresses and ports it holds
failure_modes:
  - ignoring the empty endpoint list and debugging the application instead
related:
  - k8s.service
  - k8s.probe.readiness
  - k8s.labels-selectors
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/services-networking/endpoint-slices/
